From c35f7b76c771a6b7e3c197c425fc95283653fb31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 12:14:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11280/11362] The attention line mixes events with backlog; one
 count cannot say both

Applied last hour's finding to the other attention kind and got the opposite
answer. Both come from the same 00:04Z burst, but the orphaned server resolved
itself (pid gone, port free) while the 17 audit findings do not self-resolve and
no triage record exists anywhere under ops/. So the same rendering is misleading
for event-shaped kinds and correct for backlog-shaped ones, with nothing telling
the reader which is which.

This narrows the fix queued at 15:15Z. Labelling the window is necessary and not
sufficient: calling the audit-finding count "events logged today" would trade one
wrong reading for another, since it is a standing backlog. The renderer has to
distinguish the shapes, or resolve each kind against its own live evidence -- a
pid, a port, a triage record -- rather than counting log rows.

Also records as measured, not assumed, that the 17 findings are genuinely
untriaged: no file matching triage or audit_finding exists in ops/.

